    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Given that the perimeter of a square is 32 feet, we first need to find the side length of the square. \n\nThe formula for the perimeter \\(P\\) of a square with side length \\(s\\) is:\n\\[\nP = 4s\n\\]\n\nWe know the perimeter is 32 feet, so we can set up the equation:\n\\[\n4s = 32\n\\]\n\nTo find \\(s\\), we divide both sides of the equation by 4:\n\\[\ns = \\frac{32}{4} = 8 \\text{ feet}\n\\]\n\nNext, we use the formula for the area \\(A\\) of a square, which is:\n\\[\nA = s^2\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the side length \\(s = 8\\) feet into the area formula gives:\n\\[\nA = 8^2 = 64 \\text{ square feet}\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of the square is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{64}\n\\]",
